        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9e8c8327-c0fc-53f1-aa63-370c4418b2a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nivek Ogre, Frank Sinatra, Martin Atkins, Kevin Crompton, Dave Ogilvie\n- Organizations: Skinny Puppy, Invisible Records\n- Projects: Rx\n- Roles: musicians, actors, producer, performance artist\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Sinatra, born Francis Albert Sinatra on December 12, 1915, was an American singer, actor, and producer who became one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\n- Frank Sinatra released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\n- Frank Sinatra's career was revived in 1953 by the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", and his performance won the Academy Award and Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\n- Nivek Ogre was born Kevin Graham Ogilvie on December 5, 1962, and is a Canadian musician, performance artist, and actor.\n- Nivek Ogre is best known as a founding member of the industrial music group Skinny Puppy.\n- Nivek Ogre used his alias partly because Skinny Puppy also included Kevin Crompton, also known as cEvin Key, and was produced by Dave Ogilvie, also known as Rave.\n- Rx was a one-off side project created by Skinny Puppy member Nivek Ogre in collaboration with Invisible Records founder Martin Atkins.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4c0c9f72-5765-5e45-a485-05aa64b5a053",
        "text": "Page: Nivek Ogre. Sentence: Nivek Ogre (born Kevin Graham Ogilvie December 5, 1962) is a Canadian musician, performance artist and actor best known as a founding member of the industrial music group Skinny Puppy.\nPage: Nivek Ogre. Sentence: Since that band featured another Kevin (Crompton, a.k.a. cEvin Key) and was produced by another Ogilvie (Dave, a.k.a. Rave), Ogre's alias was practical as well as theatrical.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: Francis Albert Sinatra ( ; ] ; December 12, 1915 – May 14, 1998) was an American singer, actor, and producer who was one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: He released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: His career was reborn in 1953 with the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", with his performance subsequently winning an Academy Award and Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\nPage: Rx (band). Sentence: ℞ or Rx was a one-off side project by Skinny Puppy band member Nivek Ogre, in collaboration with Invisible Records founder Martin Atkins.",
